531 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1193 0 R
/E ( Both projects involve AI/ML components \(summarisation, literacy risk prediction\) whose behaviour and accuracy are hard to predict upfront thus a fixed one-shot plan is unrealistic.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1194 0 R
/E ( User testing is explicitly listed as a deliverable, implying feedback loops are expected. This means the team gets real feedback on whether the output is actually useful and understandable to non-technical users which cannot be validated through planning alone. The project adapts based on this feedback in each subsequent iteration.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1195 0 R
/E (Since these are student projects with a hard submission deadline, the Iterative Model's time-boxing ensures that if a feature takes longer than expected, it is deferred to the next iteration rather than delaying the entire project. This keeps the team on track and ensures a working product is always available at the end of each cycle, even if not all features are complete.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1196 0 R
/E (These are student projects with a fixed scope and deadline hence the frequent requirement change assumption of Agile methods like Scrum/XP is unsuitable.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
